\title{Sums of eigenspaces are direct}
\taxon{Remark}
\date{2022-10-01}
\author{JB00}
\import{macros}

\p{We have proved the following: if #{\lambda_1, \ldots, \lambda_k} are #{k} distinct evals of #{\alpha}, then}

##{\sum_{i=1}^k V_{\lambda_i} = \bigoplus_{i=1}^k V_{\lambda_i}}

\p{is always true (and we know the projectors). This means that the only way diagonalisation fails is if}

##{\bigoplus_{i=1}^k V_{\lambda_i} = \sum_{j=1}^k V_{\lambda_j} < V \quad \text{(a strict subspace)}.}
